 Ansible Adhoc Commands
Sometimes we don’t need a full playbook.
We just need to run a quick command on multiple servers.
That’s where Ansible Adhoc commands help.
Example:
Check uptime on all servers
ansible all -m command -a "uptime"
Install package
ansible web -m yum -a "name=nginx state=present"
Simple. Fast. Powerful.
Perfect for quick operations in production.
